null},"comments":18,"created_at":"2026-07-24T18:26:51Z","updated_at":"2026-10-18T16:44:44Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible after https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121387\n\n### System information\n\nAndroid\n\n### Issue description\n\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121387 enables changing orientation in Project Manager.\nNow, if I launch the app in landscape mode and then rotate the device to portrait mode, the Project Manager does not resize properly, as shown in the video below. Note that, on the Android side, we do send a resize notification with the updated screen width and height.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/dceb309a-0e80-4899-a2cf-4582f40ae8e8\n\nIf I set `custom_scale` to `1.72` and launch the app in portrait mode, the issue does not reproduce, regardless of how many times I switch to landscape and then back to portrait. However, for same scale (1.72) if I launch the app initially in landscape mode and then rotate to portrait, the UI gets cut off.\n\nSo, the issue only occurs when the app is initially launched in landscape, where there is significantly more available horizontal space, and then switched to portrait, where the available width is much smaller. My suspicion is that somewhere in the code, a Control node's size or minimum size is being calculated or fixed based on the initial screen width and is not being properly updated when the window is resized.\n\nI also found that the issue only occurs at certain editor scale values. For me, it reproduces with `1.72`, but not with `1.75` (175%) (notice i actually increased the scale).\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Open the Android Editor initially in landscape mode and then switch to portrait mode.\n- The UI will most likely be cut off in portrait mode. (this is not guaranteed, as the issue only occurs at certain scale values, and the editor may automatically select a scale that does not reproduce the issue)\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nNA","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121726/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121726/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}